## Why This Is Asked
Tests incident-response planning across Defender for Cloud, Azure AD, Key Vault, and cross-subscription governance.

## Key Concepts
- Automated incident response playbooks
- Key Vault secret rotation
- Managed identities and service principals
- Canary rollouts and rollback strategies
- Cross-subscription isolation and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Rotate secret using Node.js Azure SDK
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SecretClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-secrets');
const vault = new SecretClient(`https://${'ProdKV'}.vault.azure.net`, new DefaultAzureCredential());
async function rotate(){ const newVal = require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64');
  await vault.setSecret('dbPassword', newVal);
}
rotate().catch(console.error);
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assess hands-on orchestration across Azure components during incidents, focusing on tenant isolation, automated rollback safety, and auditable controls.

## Key Concepts
- UEBA-driven automation (Defender for Cloud/Sentinel)
- Per-tenant network isolation (NSG, Private Endpoint)
- Key Vault key rotation and re-encryption
- Token revocation and Conditional Access control
- Canary-based rollback mechanisms
- Centralized auditing and alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator snippet
async function quarantineTenant(tenantId){
  await applyPerTenantNSG(tenantId);
  await rotateKeyVaultKeys(tenantId);
  await revokeTokensAndDisableCA(tenantId);
  await rollbackToLastGoodRelease(tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assess storage security, policy enforcement, and rollback capabilities in a practical scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy deny public network access
- Private Endpoints and VNET integration
- Managed Identities RBAC
- Secrets in Key Vault instead of config

## Code Example
```json
{
  "mode": "Indexed",
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "properties.publicNetworkAccess", "equals": "Enabled"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate rollback after applying policy?
- How would you handle temporary public access needs during migrations?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical guardrail design across multi-subscription data platforms, focusing real-world constraints like admin elevation, secrets hygiene, data egress controls, governance, monitoring, and rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Least-privilege RBAC with PIM
- Key Vault secrets + policy gating
- Private Link / firewall-based egress controls
- Data governance and DLP
- UEBA with Azure Sentinel
- Canary deployments and GitOps rollback

## Code Example

```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Web/sites" },
        { "anyOf": [
          { "field": "siteConfig.appSettings[*].value", "like": "*SECRET*" },
          { "field": "siteConfig.connectionStrings[*].value", "like": "*SECRET*" }
        ] }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify the guardrail without affecting production?
- What telemetry and alerting would prove efficacy and catch anomalies quickly?

